---
layout: survey.njk
title: "Street surveys — velocity.report"
permalink: /surveys/index.html
description: Measured road-user behaviour at fixed street sites in San Francisco, from the velocity.report LiDAR perception pipeline. No cameras, faces or plates. Results are a research preview.
---
{#
  Survey listing: map above a table of sites. Every row is rendered here
  from src/_data/surveys.js; survey-page.js adds search, filters and
  sorting. While each site has one recording, the table leaves out the
  latest-recording and recording-count columns and the year chips, and the
  page states no site or recording totals. Filter chips appear only when
  they would separate something: a "multiple recordings" chip once a site
  has two, a sensor chip once radar and LiDAR surveys are both listed, and a
  measurement chip per family once there is more than one.
#}
{% import "survey/macros.njk" as sv %}

<style>

  .scenes__map { border: 1px solid rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.28); border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem; margin-bottom: 0.6rem; }
  .scenes__map svg { display: block; }
  /* This is set synchronously before the large no-JS SVG is parsed. Leaflet
     replaces it; hiding it up front prevents one painted frame of labels. */
  .scene-map-js #scene-map > .scene-map { visibility: hidden; }
  .scenes__mapframe { position: relative; }
  #scene-map { height: 520px; border-radius: 3px; background: #dcebef; }
  #scene-map .leaflet-popup-content { font-size: 0.9rem; }
  #scene-map .scene-map__site-shimmer.is-shimmering {
    animation: scene-map-site-shimmer 450ms ease-in-out var(--scene-map-shimmer-delay) both;
  }
  @keyframes scene-map-site-shimmer {
    0%, 100% { fill-opacity: 0; }
    50% { fill-opacity: 0.82; }
  }
  .scenes__load-map { position: absolute; z-index: 700; left: 0.65rem; bottom: 0.65rem; border: 1px solid #536b74; border-radius: 3px; padding: 0.42rem 0.7rem; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92); color: #183039; font: inherit; font-size: 0.8rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .scenes__load-map[aria-checked="true"] { border-color: #047857; background: rgba(4, 120, 87, 0.94); color: white; }
  .scenes__load-map[hidden], .scenes__consent[hidden] { display: none; }
  .scenes__consent { position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 900; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; padding: 1rem; background: rgba(3, 9, 12, 0.72); }
  .scenes__consent-card { width: min(31rem, 100%); border: 1px solid #536b74; border-radius: 4px; padding: 1.15rem; background: #0b1013; color: #e2edf0; box-shadow: 0 12px 42px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5); }
  .scenes__consent-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: start; gap: 1rem; }
  .scenes__consent h2 { margin: 0; font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .scenes__consent p { font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .scenes__consent-close { border: 0; background: none; color: inherit; font-size: 1.35rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .scenes__consent-actions { display: flex; justify-content: end; gap: 0.5rem; margin-top: 1rem; }
  .scenes__consent-actions button { border: 1px solid #61777f; border-radius: 3px; padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; background: transparent; color: inherit; font: inherit; cursor: pointer; }
  .scenes__consent-actions [data-action="allow"] { background: #047857; border-color: #047857; color: white; }
  #scene-map .leaflet-hitRegions-pane path { cursor: pointer; }
  #scene-map .leaflet-cellFill-pane,
  #scene-map .leaflet-grid-pane,
  #scene-map .leaflet-markers-pane { pointer-events: none; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    #scene-map .scene-map__site-shimmer { animation: none; }
  }
  /* The survey pages are dark throughout, so the map always takes its dark styling. */
  @media all {
    #scene-map { background: #172126; }
    #scene-map .scene-map-cycle-tiles { filter: invert(1) hue-rotate(180deg) brightness(0.78) contrast(0.9); }
    #scene-map .leaflet-bar a,
    #scene-map .leaflet-popup-content-wrapper,
    #scene-map .leaflet-popup-tip,
    #scene-map .leaflet-control-attribution { background: #172126; color: #d5e3e8; }
    #scene-map .leaflet-bar a:hover { background: #263940; }
    #scene-map .leaflet-control-attribution a,
    #scene-map .leaflet-popup-content a { color: #75d5e8; }
    #scene-map .leaflet-tooltip { background: #172126; color: #d5e3e8; border-color: #536b74; }
  }
  .scenes__mapnote { font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.7; margin: 0 0 1.75rem; max-width: 68ch; }


     is little enough that a half-width box was mostly empty and the listing


</style>

<div class="sv-wrap sv-list" data-survey-list>
  <header class="sv-list__head">
    <div class="sv-stack">
      <h1 class="sv-list__title">Street surveys</h1>
      <p class="sv-list__lede">Measured road-user behaviour at fixed sites. No cameras, faces or plates. Results are a research preview: the LiDAR tracker still splits some tracks and produces unstable trails.</p>
    </div>
    {% if surveys.pipeline.build %}<p class="sv-mono sv-list__pipeline">pipeline <span class="sv-em">{{ surveys.pipeline.build }}</span></p>{% endif %}
  </header>

  <div class="sv-filters" role="search">
    <label class="sv-search">
      <span class="sv-sr">Search surveys</span>
      <span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span>
      <input type="search" placeholder="Street, intersection or cell" autocomplete="off" data-site-search>
    </label>
    {% if surveys.families.length > 1 %}{% for family in surveys.families %}
      <button type="button" class="sv-chip" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="family:{{ family.id }}">Has: {{ family.name }}</button>
    {% endfor %}{% endif %}
    {% if surveys.sensorKinds.length > 1 %}{% for k in surveys.sensorKinds %}
      <button type="button" class="sv-chip" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="sensor:{{ k }}">{{ surveys.sensors[k].label }}</button>
    {% endfor %}{% endif %}
    {% if surveys.totals.multi %}<button type="button" class="sv-chip" aria-pressed="false" data-filter="multi">Multiple recordings</button>{% endif %}
  </div>

  <div class="sv-list__layout">
    <div class="sv-list__map">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css"
            integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
      <div class="scenes__map">
        <div class="scenes__mapframe">
          <script>document.documentElement.classList.add("scene-map-js");</script>
          <div id="scene-map" data-coastline-url="{{ '/img/maps/sf-coastline.geojson.gz' | url }}">
            {# No-JS fallback: the self-contained S2 diagram makes no network request. #}
            {% include "scene-map.svg" %}
          </div>
          <button id="scene-map-load" class="scenes__load-map" type="button" hidden>Load Cycle map</button>
          <div id="scene-map-consent" class="scenes__consent" role="presentation" hidden>
            <div class="scenes__consent-card" role="alertdialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="scene-map-consent-title">
              <div class="scenes__consent-head">
                <h2 id="scene-map-consent-title">Download Cycle map data?</h2>
                <button type="button" class="scenes__consent-close" data-action="close" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
              </div>
              <p>This will request CyclOSM map tiles from OSM France. Your IP address and the map area being viewed will be sent to that external service.</p>
              <p>The local coastline, S2 cells and survey points remain available if you cancel.</p>
              <p>Your choice is remembered in this browser. You can switch the Cycle map off later; cached tiles stay in the browser, but no new map tiles are requested until you switch it on again.</p>
              <div class="scenes__consent-actions">
                <button type="button" data-action="cancel">Cancel</button>
                <button type="button" data-action="allow">Download Cycle map</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      {# The site list travels in a script block, not an attribute: a place name
         with an apostrophe in it — Fisherman's Wharf — ends a quoted attribute
         early, and the JSON arrives truncated. #}
      <script type="application/json" id="scene-map-data">{{ scenes.sites | dump | replace("<", "\\u003c") | safe }}</script>
      <script src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js"
              integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
      <script type="module" src="{{ '/js/scene-map.js' | url }}"></script>
    </div>

    <div class="sv-list__sites">
      <div class="sv-tablewrap">
        <table class="sv-sitetable">
          <caption class="sv-sr">Survey sites. Sort by a column; sites missing a value sort last, never as zero.</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" data-sort="name" aria-sort="ascending"><button type="button">Site</button></th>
              <th scope="col">Speed distribution</th>
              <th scope="col" data-sort="p85"><button type="button">P85 / limit</button></th>
              <th scope="col" data-sort="over"><button type="button">≥ limit</button></th>
              <th scope="col" data-sort="count"><button type="button">Tracks</button></th>
              <th scope="col" data-sort="minutes"><button type="button">Min</button></th>
              {% if surveys.families.length > 1 %}<th scope="col" data-sort="familyCount"><button type="button">Measurements</button></th>{% endif %}
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody data-site-tbody>
            {% for site in surveys.sites %}
              {% set v = site | surveyView(site.speedLimitMph) %}
              {% set r = v.latest %}
              <tr data-site-row data-site="{{ site.id }}" data-name="{{ site.title }}" data-cell="{{ site.cell or '' }}"
                  data-recordings="{{ site.recordings.length }}" data-sensors="{{ site.sensors | join(' ') }}" data-families="{{ site.families | join(' ') }}"
                  data-years="{{ site.years | join(" ") }}"
                  data-p85="{{ r.speed.p85 if r and r.speed else '' }}"
                  data-over="{{ r.over if r and r.over !== null else '' }}" data-count="{{ r.speed.count if r and r.speed else '' }}"
                  data-minutes="{{ r.when.minutes if r else '' }}" data-family-count="{{ site.families.length }}">
                <th scope="row">{% if site.published and site.page %}<a href="{{ site.page }}">{{ site.title }}</a>{% else %}{{ site.title }}{% endif %}{% if site.cell %} <span class="sv-mono sv-small">{{ site.cell }}</span>{% endif %}</th>
                <td>{{ r.charts.spark | safe if r and r.charts }}</td>
                <td class="sv-mono">{% if r and r.speed %}{{ r.speed.p85 | fixed1 }}{% if v.limit %}<span class="sv-muted"> / {{ v.limit }}</span>{% endif %}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
                <td class="sv-mono">{{ r.overText if r else "—" }}</td>
                <td class="sv-mono">{{ r.speed.count if r and r.speed else "—" }}</td>
                <td class="sv-mono">{{ r.when.minutes if r else "—" }}</td>
                {% if surveys.families.length > 1 %}<td class="sv-mono">{{ site.families.length }}/{{ surveys.families.length }}</td>{% endif %}
              </tr>
            {% endfor %}
          </tbody>
        </table>
        <p class="sv-note">Sort by any measured column; there is no combined score. Sites missing a value sort last, never as zero. The ≥ limit column stays empty until a site's posted limit is recorded.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="sv-note" data-site-empty hidden>No surveys match. Clear the search or filters to see every site.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sv-list__notes">
  <p class="scenes__mapnote">
      Not every site here has a published recording; the rest are places the
      sensor has been, shown so the map
      answers where it has been rather than only what there is to watch.
      With permission, the background uses cycling routes from
      <a href="https://www.cyclosm.org/">CyclOSM</a>, hosted by OSM France, and
      follows your device's light or dark appearance. Without it, the local
      coastline and S2 geometry remain.
      Each point is one recorded site. Click it for the name and, where there is a
      recording, a link to it. Points carry no labels on the map: at this zoom a
      label covers the street it stands on, and the street is the thing worth
      seeing. Each site is listed below with its S2 level
      {{ scenes.levels.neighbourhood }} cell, about a kilometre across, under a
      heading for the level {{ scenes.levels.area }} area that contains it.
    </p>

  <p class="scenes__index">
      The cells come from <a href="https://s2geometry.io/">S2</a>, which divides the
      globe into a hierarchy of cells and names each one with a token. A token is
      shown here as <code>80858-0f4</code>, hyphenated only to make the shared prefix
      easy to compare; the hyphen carries no meaning and the canonical token is
      <code>808580f4</code>. Every token on this page is derived from the survey's
      recorded position, so a cell and the position it indexes cannot disagree.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
<script type="module" src="/js/survey-page.js"></script>
